    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesn't feel like a gift. it feels like i'm just a ghost wandering around a house that doesn't belong to me anymore. he was the color in everything. now everything is just gray. i look at his side of the bed and it just hurts so much it feels physical. i don't want to \"fill the space\" with something else. i just want the hurting to stop.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—grief isn't a lesson to learn, it's a wound that won't stop bleeding. The gray is real, and the physical ache is your body mourning what your mind can't accept. You don't have to fill anything or find meaning; you just have to survive the next hour, then the next. And if the hurting never stops, that's okay—it means you loved him enough to break, and that's not weakness, that's proof.",
